== About Me
I am an assistant professor in the School of Mathematical Sciences and Center for Machine Learning Research at Peking University.

Previously, I was a postdoctoral researcher at  Princeton University and the University of Pennsylvania.
I received my Ph.D. in computational mathematics from Peking University in 2018, advised by Prof. [https://web.math.princeton.edu/~weinan/ Weinan E], and my B.S. in mathematics from Nankai University in 2012.

I aim to develop a *predictive science of deep learning* by combining mathematical analysis with large-scale training experiments. My current focus is on understanding LLM pretraining.  For more, see my [research.html research overview] and [doc/LLM-pretraining-theory.pdf talk slides on functional scaling laws].


== Recruiting

We welcome postdocs, PhD students, and undergraduates interested in the scientific foundations of AI. I recruit PhD students through both the School of Mathematical Sciences and the Center for Machine Learning Research (CMLR). 

If you are interested in joining us, please email me your CV and a brief description of your research interests.

== Recent Updates

- 2026-09:  [https://neurips.cc/virtual/2026/loc/sydney/poster/150706 When and how signSGD outperforms SGD: a functional scaling law perspective] accepted to *NeurIPS 2026 (Spotlight)*. 

- 2026-08: New preprints on [https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.24814 effective learning rate (ELR) collapse] and [https://arxiv.org/abs/2609.02728 momentum in large-batch training] are now available on arXiv.

- 2026-07: I taught a short course on /Foundations of Deep Learning: Approximation, Generalization, and Scaling/ at [https://yingzhouli.com/others/FDUSS2026/index-mass-en.html 2026 Fudan University International Summer School on AI in Math].

- 2026-07: Co-organized the [https://ml-math-2026.github.io/ 2026 PKU Workshop on Mathematical Foundations of Modern Machine Learning] with [https://www.lfhsgre.org/ Fanghui Liu] and [https://kunyuan827.github.io/ Kun Yuan].

- 2026-06: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.06797 Optimal learning-rate schedules under functional scaling laws: power decay and warmup-stable-decay] accepted to *COLT 2026*.

- 2026-06: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.24275 GradPower: powering gradients for faster language model pre-training] accepted to *ICML 2026*.

- 2026-02: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.19691 Smoothness adaptivity in constant-depth neural networks: optimal rates via smooth activations] released on arXiv.

- 2026-02: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.14208 Fast catch-up, late switching: optimal batch size scheduling via functional scaling laws] accepted to *ICLR 2026*.

- 2025-09: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.19189 Functional scaling laws in kernel regression: loss dynamics and learning rate schedules] accepted to *NeurIPS 2025 (Spotlight)*.

- 2025-06: [https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.19002 The sharpness disparity principle in transformers for accelerating language model pre-training] accepted to *ICML 2025*.

